---
title: Snippet page
layout: home
description: One file, open in the editor, with the rest of the folder beside it. Full width, no widget rail — the only navigation a reader of a snippet wants is the other snippets.
eyebrow: Collections · Snippets
source: src/components/editor.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Snippets · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-with-aside im-with-aside-start im-wrap-wide" style="--im-aside-width: 15rem">
	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<nav class="im-filetree" aria-label="Snippets">
				<p class="im-filetree-head">Snippets</p>
				<p class="im-filetree-group">{{icon "folder"}}css</p>
				{{#each demo.snippets}}{{#match lang "=" "CSS"}}<a class="im-filetree-file" href="/collections/snippets/page/" style="--im-repo-lang: {{langColor}}"{{#match @index "=" 0}} aria-current="page"{{/match}}>{{icon "file-code"}}{{file}}</a>{{/match}}{{/each}}
				<p class="im-filetree-group">{{icon "folder"}}js</p>
				{{#each demo.snippets}}{{#match lang "=" "JavaScript"}}<a class="im-filetree-file" href="/collections/snippets/page/" style="--im-repo-lang: {{langColor}}">{{icon "file-code"}}{{file}}</a>{{/match}}{{/each}}
				<p class="im-filetree-group">{{icon "folder"}}hbs</p>
				{{#each demo.snippets}}{{#match lang "=" "Handlebars"}}<a class="im-filetree-file" href="/collections/snippets/page/" style="--im-repo-lang: {{langColor}}">{{icon "file-code"}}{{file}}</a>{{/match}}{{/each}}
			</nav>
		</div>
	</aside>

	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 1.75rem">
		{{#with demo.snippets.[0]}}
		<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
			<ol class="im-breadcrumb im-breadcrumb-chevron">
				<li><a href="/">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a></li>
				<li><a href="/collections/snippets/">{{> "icons/code"}}<span>Snippets</span></a></li>
				<li><span aria-current="page">{{file}}</span></li>
			</ol>
		</nav>

		<header class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: .625rem">
			<p class="im-snipcard-meta"><span class="im-kind" data-kind="post">{{> "icons/code"}}Snippet</span><span>{{lang}}</span><span>Last checked 14 September 2026</span></p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">{{name}}</h1>
			<p class="im-lede" style="margin: 0">{{text}}</p>
		</header>

		<figure class="im-editor im-mock im-mock-mac im-mock-lights" style="--im-editor-max: none; --im-repo-lang: {{langColor}}">
			<div class="im-mock-bar">
				<span class="im-mock-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
				<div class="im-mock-tabs">
					<button class="im-mock-tab" type="button" aria-current="page">{{file}}</button>
					<button class="im-mock-tab" type="button" data-dirty>scratch.css</button>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="im-editor-body">
				<pre class="im-editor-lines" aria-hidden="true">{{lines}}</pre>
				<pre><code class="language-{{lang_class}}">{{snippet}}</code></pre>
			</div>
			<p class="im-editor-status">
				<span class="im-editor-lang">{{lang}}</span>
				<span>UTF-8</span>
				<span>LF</span>
				<span class="im-editor-push">Ln 1, Col 1</span>
				<button class="im-editor-copy" type="button" data-im-copy="{{snippet}}" data-im-copied-label="Copied">{{icon "copy"}}<span data-im-copy-label>Copy</span></button>
			</p>
		</figure>
		{{/with}}

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush">
			<h2>Why it is written this way</h2>
			<p>A media query picks a size and then jumps to another one. <code>clamp()</code> gives a minimum, a preferred value and a maximum, and every size between them is a real size — including the window widths nobody wrote a breakpoint for.</p>
			<p>The middle term is the part worth reading. <code>0.9rem + 0.5vw</code> rather than <code>2.5vw</code> alone: a pure viewport unit means a reader who zooms gets nothing, because <code>vw</code> does not respond to zoom the way <code>rem</code> does. Mixing a <code>rem</code> into the preferred value is what keeps the text honest at 200%.</p>

			<h2>When not to</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Not for a heading that must not shrink.</strong> A minimum of <code>1rem</code> is a promise; check it at 320px before you make it.</li>
				<li><strong>Not on <code>line-height</code>.</strong> Fluid leading drifts out of the vertical rhythm and there is no way to get it back.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<div class="im-snipcards" style="--im-snipcards-min: 22rem">
			{{#each demo.snippets}}{{#match @index ">" 3}}{{> "components/snippet-card"}}{{/match}}{{/each}}
		</div>
	</article>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>No sidebar, and no copy button</h2>
		<p>Two deliberate absences.</p>
		<p><strong>No widget rail.</strong> An author card, a newsletter box and a "popular posts" list are things a reader of an <em>essay</em> might want next. A reader who arrived at <code>fluid-type.css</code> wants the other files, which is why the left column is a file tree and the page is otherwise full width.</p>
		<p><strong>Copy lives on this page only.</strong> In the grid the code is selectable and nothing more — a copy button on a card invites skipping the paragraph that explains the code. Here, where the explanation is, the status bar has one.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-editor</code></td><td>The window. It reuses <a href="/content/mockups/">the mockup chrome</a> — <code>im-mock im-mock-mac im-mock-lights</code> — rather than drawing a second one.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-editor-lines</code></td><td>The gutter, as ONE block of numbers rather than a counter per line: a counter numbers the wrap, and code wraps. It is <code>position: sticky</code> so it survives a sideways scroll.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-editor-status</code></td><td>Language, encoding, position. The row that makes it read as an editor and not as a terminal.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-filetree</code></td><td>The other files. <code>aria-current="page"</code> is the open one, drawn with the same fill-and-weight active state as every other list in the system.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-snipcard</code></td><td>The card: the sentence above, the window below.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>The highlighter leaves it alone</h2>
		<p><code>im-code.js</code> normally wraps a <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> in its own figure with a title bar and a copy button. Inside <code>.im-editor</code> it colours the tokens and stops — otherwise the card would have two title bars and the button this page exists to not have. <code>data-im-bare</code> on any <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code> does the same thing anywhere else.</p>

		<h2>Code does not wrap</h2>
		<p><code>white-space: pre</code>, and the body scrolls sideways. A wrapped line of CSS is a different line of CSS, and a reader who cannot tell where line 2 ends cannot use the snippet. The gutter stays put while it scrolls.</p>
	</div>
</section>
